1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,062
These two services can't finish starting.

2
00:00:02,142 --> 00:00:03,680
Spring starts Service A,

3
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:05,668
whose constructor needs Service B.

4
00:00:05,748 --> 00:00:08,100
But Service B needs Service A first.

5
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:10,820
The arguments must exist before construction.

6
00:00:10,820 --> 00:00:12,840
Neither constructor can finish.

7
00:00:12,920 --> 00:00:14,340
Startup fails with a bean

8
00:00:14,340 --> 00:00:16,680
currently in creation exception.

9
00:00:16,680 --> 00:00:18,568
This is a constructor cycle.

10
00:00:18,648 --> 00:00:20,380
Refactor the collaboration.

11
00:00:20,380 --> 00:00:22,960
An orchestration service calls A and B;

12
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:25,057
they no longer depend on each other.

13
00:00:25,137 --> 00:00:27,020
Our tests confirm failure before,

14
00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:28,880
and successful startup after.

15
00:00:28,880 --> 00:00:32,000
Other circular references behave differently.

16
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:34,350
Redesign the dependency graph.

17
00:00:36,350 --> 00:00:37,441
Thanks for watching.

